  <p>Weight loss fundamentally boils down to energy balance. If you consume fewer calories than your body burns, you enter a physiological state known as a <strong>caloric deficit</strong>. But exactly how many calories should you cut? Health experts and scientific literature generally recommend a gradual and steady weight loss of 0.5 to 1 kilogram (1 to 2 pounds) per week. This ensures long-term sustainability and minimizes the risk of metabolic adaptation.</p>

  

  
